## Step 1 (Block 2 — `Certificación`): `Conglomerado` (`grupo_empresarial`) — Unskippable Prerequisite

* **Domain Concept:** A parent bucket above `organizacion` (`organizacion.id_grupo_empresarial FK`). It groups organizations together in a shared environment regardless of formal legal relationship so their certificates can later be linked.
* **Lifecycle & Rules:**
* Every `organizacion` can belong to a `grupo_empresarial`. By default, when an organization is standalone ("alone"), it has its own auto-created/1:1 `grupo_empresarial` whose `nombre` / `etiqueta` defaults to the organization's `nombre`.
* **Seamless Re-bucketing / Merging:** A standalone organization can be reassigned/joined into another `grupo_empresarial` at any time without friction. When an organization leaves its previous `grupo_empresarial` and that previous bucket becomes empty (`0` active organizations), the system must automatically archive/clean up that empty bucket (or prompt/auto-archive it safely via soft-delete) so orphan single-org buckets do not clutter the system.
* **Multi View & Filters:** Include smart filters/facets in `Conglomerado` (and `Organización`) to easily identify standalone/single-org buckets ("Organizaciones solas / sin agrupar") vs multi-org conglomerates, plus quick-action workflows to merge/move an organization into an existing conglomerate.
* **Pipeline Gate (Unskippable):** Organizations/certificates cannot appear or be operated on in Step 2 (`Vínculo`) unless their organization belongs to a valid active `grupo_empresarial`.



